From fa00772bc31939d4a15a3c51e83c326c3c2907cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <dev@phlink.local>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:42:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.02e UpdateCheckPipeline (orchestrator)

Adds phlink::updater::UpdateCheckPipeline: a one-shot orchestrator that
runs a full update-check round end-to-end:

  1. Parse + verify the trust-pinned root.json with TufClient.
  2. Drive MetadataFetcher (timestamp -> snapshot -> targets).
  3. Look up the target for the running platform/arch/version.
  4. Drive PayloadFetcher (download + length + sha256 verify).
  5. Write staged.json so the platform helper (10-03/04/05) can
     pick the payload up at next launch.

Outcomes: kOk, kUpToDate, kMetadataError, kTargetMissing,
kPayloadError, kIoError.

This is the production CheckCallback that will be bound into
UpdaterService once a settings WebUI handler asks for it (deferred to
plan 10-06; we don't want to touch chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_*
for a lazy-built KeyedService that nothing user-visible references
yet).

Also extends metadata_test_helpers with BuildTargetsSignedWithEntry()
so tests can pin a specific target name + length + sha256.

26/26 phlink_updater_unittests pass (4 new pipeline tests).
Refs phlink phase 10-02e.
